[0.601, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[22.129, "o", "- I built the Weather CLI queue item: `bin/weather.js` and `src/weather.js` have no dependencies. `weather <city>` looks the city up through Open-Meteo's geocoding API, then prints the current temperature.\r\n- `--units metric|imperial` defaults to metric. It accepts `--units x` and `--units=x`, multi-word city names, and gives clear errors for bad units, a missing city, or an unknown city.\r\n- I added `package.json` with `npm test`, six `node:test` tests in `test/weather.test.js`, and a README with usage examples. The tests pass (6/6) against a mocked fetch, so I didn't call the live API.\r\n- I set the local git identity to ana / ana@example.invalid and committed `8dc00bc` on `feat/weather-units`. I didn't push.\r\n- I left the \"plan weather-demo\" queue item and `docs/` untouched, and `docs/` stays untracked.\r\n"]
[0.479, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[0.028, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b]0;agent@4e14dcebffc6: /work\u0007agent@4e14dcebffc6:/work$ \u001b[K"]
